        h1: "Cyber Essentials Certification in Shropshire",
        intro: "Need Cyber Essentials for your Shropshire business? Whether it's a contract requirement, an insurer's nudge, or just good sense, Fresh Tech runs you through the whole thing. We're based in Ludlow, so the help is local and hands-on.",
        content: "**What Cyber Essentials actually is**\n\nCyber Essentials is the UK government's baseline cyber security scheme. It covers five technical controls. Firewalls. Secure setup of your devices and cloud services. Who can log in and what they can do. Anti-malware. And keeping software patched. Get these five right and you've stopped most of the everyday attacks that hit small businesses.\n\nThere are two tiers. Basic is a self-assessment - you fill in a long questionnaire and an assessor checks it. Plus is the same scope but with an external technical audit and a hands-on scan. Plus carries more weight with insurers and larger buyers. We'll tell you honestly which one you actually need.\n\n**Why so many Shropshire firms now need it**\n\nGovernment work all but requires it. Defence supply chains demand it. NHS framework contracts ask for it. Many insurers offer better rates - or only cover you at all - if you hold the badge. And bigger clients are starting to ask suppliers to prove their basics are in order.\n\nWe see this across the county. Manufacturers in Telford bidding on MOD-adjacent work. Solicitors in Shrewsbury meeting SRA guidance. Farms and rural firms across the Marches handling client data. Each one wants the same thing: get certified, get back to work.\n\n**Our process, in plain English**\n\nStep one - we run a gap analysis. We look at your current setup and write down exactly where you fall short.\n\nStep two - we fix the gaps. The trade calls this 'remediation', which just means putting things right. Patching old software. Tightening firewalls. Cleaning up old admin accounts. Turning on multi-factor login.\n\nStep three - we prepare your answers, submit your application, and get you certified. With our [Cyber Essentials](/services/cyber-essentials) service every fix is included in the fixed quote. No hourly bills creeping up.\n\n**Why we fix the gaps first**\n\nWe never submit until the gaps are closed. That's it. Some firms charge to do the questionnaire, fail you, then charge again to fix things. We don't work that way. You pay one fee. We only submit when our certification partner says you're ready to pass.\n\n**Staying certified, year after year**\n\nCyber Essentials needs renewing every twelve months. If you're on our [Managed IT Support](/services/managed-it-support) the controls stay in place all year. Renewal is paperwork, not a panic. Most clients get re-certified in days, not weeks.\n\nWant a free, honest second opinion on where you stand? Book a [gap check](/contact) with us. No hard sell.",
