        location: "Kidderminster",
        isCounty: false,
        title: "Microsoft 365 Support Kidderminster",
        metaDesc: "Microsoft 365 support for Kidderminster and Wyre Forest businesses. Migration, security, Teams, SharePoint. Expert management at SMB-friendly prices.",
        h1: "Microsoft 365 Support for Kidderminster Businesses",
        intro: "Kidderminster and Wyre Forest firms deserve Microsoft 365 that's set up properly, locked down, and genuinely useful. Fresh Tech handles the lot - from the first migration to the day-to-day care - at prices that work for small firms.",
        content: "**Microsoft 365 that works as hard as you do**\n\nKidderminster firms are practical and results-focused. Your Microsoft 365 setup should be the same. Not bloated with features no one uses. Not left on weak default settings. Not costing more than it needs to.\n\nOur [Microsoft 365](/services/microsoft-365-business) service is built for firms like yours. We set up the platform for what your team actually does. We turn on the safety tools you're already paying for. And we cut out the jargon. The aim is simple: tech that works, and stops getting in the way.\n\n**Microsoft 365 plans in plain English**\n\nThere are three main plans for small firms. Business Basic gives you web-only email and Teams - around five pounds per user per month at typical list prices. Business Standard adds installed Word, Excel, and Outlook for around ten pounds. Business Premium adds device management, Conditional Access, and anti-phishing tools for around eighteen pounds.\n\nFor most Wyre Forest firms, Premium is the right plan. The two mistakes we see most often? Firms on Standard who really need Premium for the safety extras. And firms paying for Premium who never switched the extras on. We fix both.\n\n**What we set up**\n\n- **Email security**: Anti-phishing, anti-spam, safe attachments, and multi-factor login - which alone stops the vast majority of account hacks.\n- **Teams**: Tidy channels, video meetings, and Teams Phone to take over from old phone lines. Most firms cut phone costs by a third or more.\n- **SharePoint**: A sensible folder layout, clear permissions, and search that actually finds the file. Replaces messy shared drives and USB sticks.\n- **Intune**: Every laptop and phone managed from one screen. We push updates, set up screen locks, and wipe lost kit before it costs you.\n- **Backup**: Because Microsoft 365 does not back itself up - a fact that surprises most people we meet.\n\n**Migration made simple**\n\nIf you're moving from a legacy email host, a local file server, or another cloud setup, we handle everything. We plan the cut-over, copy every email and file, set up security from day one, and train your team. Most moves run over a weekend so your staff come in on Monday and just find things working. Better, in fact.\n\n**SMB pricing, no long lock-ins**\n\nWe're open about [pricing](/pricing). No three-year deals. No surprise invoices. For the deeper dive on plans, see our [Business Premium](/microsoft-business-premium) page.",
