        content: "**What Every New Business Needs (And What Can Wait)**\n\n**Essential From Day One:**\n- **[Microsoft 365 Business Premium](/microsoft-business-premium)** - Professional email (@yourdomain.com), Teams for communication, SharePoint for file storage, and built-in security (MFA, Intune, Defender). This single subscription replaces a dozen consumer tools.\n- **Business-Grade Laptops** - Our [Hardware Procurement](/services/hardware-procurement) service sources Dell business machines pre-configured with your company settings. Staff open the box, log in, and everything is ready.\n- **Cyber Security Basics** - [MFA](/technology/mfa) on every account, proper password policies, and endpoint protection. Non-negotiable, even for a two-person startup.\n- **Backup** - Your data needs protecting from day one. We configure [cloud backup](/services/backup-disaster-recovery) so that files, emails, and settings are automatically protected.\n\n**Nice to Have Early On:**\n- **Cloud Phone System** - A proper business phone number with a cloud-based system (Yeastar, Teams Voice, or a hosted platform). We recommend app-based calling so your number works from any device without renting desk phones.\n- **Business Internet** - If you're moving into an office, we'll source and project-manage your broadband or leased line installation.\n- **Structured Cabling & WiFi** - If your new premises need network infrastructure, we design and install [enterprise WiFi](/technology/business-networking) and structured cabling.\n\n**Can Wait Until You're Established:**\n- **[Cyber Essentials](/services/cyber-essentials) Certification** - Important for winning contracts, but you need a stable IT setup first. We can certify you once everything is bedded in.\n- **Advanced Security Tools** - [Application control](/technology/application-control), [EDR](/technology/edr-mdr), and SIEM can come later as you grow. The basics protect you now.\n\n**What Sets Us Apart for Startups**\n\nWe're a small business ourselves. We started Fresh Tech from scratch and understand the pressure of every purchasing decision when revenue is still building. We'll be honest about what you need now and what can wait. We won't sell you a server when SharePoint will do. We won't push premium licences when standard is sufficient. And our [pricing](/pricing) is designed to be affordable for growing businesses.",
